{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400007-laurel-and-ivy-technique-for-3e","id":1400007,"title":"Laurel-And-Ivy Technique for 3e","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-29T22:33:06-07:00","id":1400007,"title":"Laurel-And-Ivy Technique for 3e","content":"What prerequisites and placement would you give the 2e Knack in 3e in the Lunar Charm lists?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1546-great-cthulhu","name":"Great Cthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1546_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T22:58:47-07:00","id":1400014,"title":"","content":"3e Lunar shapeshifting is supposed to be limited to only humans and animals. That's intentional, because the 2e Lunar-style &quot;anything at all&quot; shapeshifting is something the current designers have decided broadens Lunar themes and playstyle beyond manageability, and makes shapeshifting very difficult to balance. So you're not likely to ever see Laurels-and-Ivy Technique make a reappearance in 3e.<br /> <br /> That said, if all you need is to <i>disguise</i> yourself as a plant, Lunars can do that just fine. They're still masters of disguise. Personally, I'd allow Essential Mirror Nature (Lunars, p. 156), which covers disguising yourself as a supernatural creature, to cover disguising yourself as a plant creature as well. If that doesn't suit, or if you want to disguise yourself as just a mundane, inanimate plant, a charm in the same tree should do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T23:16:31-07:00","id":1400015,"title":"","content":"This makes sense. I suppose Subtle Chameleon Practice it is then! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1546-great-cthulhu","name":"Great Cthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1546_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T01:01:10-07:00","id":1400022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400007-laurel-and-ivy-technique-for-3e?p=1400014#post1400014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3e Lunar shapeshifting is supposed to be limited to only humans and animals. That's intentional, because the 2e Lunar-style &quot;anything at all&quot; shapeshifting is something the current designers have decided broadens Lunar themes and playstyle beyond manageability, and makes shapeshifting very difficult to balance. So you're not likely to ever see Laurels-and-Ivy Technique make a reappearance in 3e.</div> </div> </div> </div>As somebody who never much cared for Lunars being able to turn into plants, I think these concerns don't need to matter too much at an individual table that likes the idea.<br /> <br /> My immediate impulse is a Universal Charm with two Hearts Blood Charms as prerequisites. A specific two; let's say... Emperor Grasshopper Form and Memory Drinking Meditation. Actually, let's add Constant Quicksilver Rearrangement in there as well, that premise of increased fine tuning to one's protean flesh seems like a logical step before.<br /> <br /> In fact, maybe forget the Heart's Blood Charms... oh wait no, Quicksilver Rearrangement isn't the one with the large number of prerequisites, and it does feel as though some Heart's Blood should be included in what is effectively a weird Heart's Blood upgrade (you should be doing <i>something</i> to internalize those plant shapes).<br /> <br /> So it's Essence 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T06:04:14-07:00","id":1400065,"title":"","content":"Another possibility that comes to mind is that Laurel-And-Ivy Technique could be a Lunar exclusive Evocation on green jade armour with similar &quot;conceal yourself in vegetation&quot; themes to Midnight Thorn. There's already a precedent for this with the Wasp of the Labyrinth Trick which used to be an Ink Monkeys era Lunar charm but is now an evocation for the Ichneumon Blades. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T06:16:16-07:00","id":1400075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400007-laurel-and-ivy-technique-for-3e?p=1400065#post1400065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another possibility that comes to mind is that Laurel-And-Ivy Technique could be a Lunar exclusive Evocation on green jade armour with similar &quot;conceal yourself in vegetation&quot; themes to Midnight Thorn. There's already a precedent for this with the Wasp of the Labyrinth Trick which used to be an Ink Monkeys era Lunar charm but is now an evocation for the Ichneumon Blades.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I've been building a set of plant-based evocations for a Wood Dragon's Claw control spell. This would be a great addition. Thanks for the suggestion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1546-great-cthulhu","name":"Great Cthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1546_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T06:17:03-07:00","id":1400077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400007-laurel-and-ivy-technique-for-3e?p=1400022#post1400022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As somebody who never much cared for Lunars being able to turn into plants, I think these concerns don't need to matter too much at an individual table that likes the idea.<br /> <br /> My immediate impulse is a Universal Charm with two Hearts Blood Charms as prerequisites. A specific two; let's say... Emperor Grasshopper Form and Memory Drinking Meditation. Actually, let's add Constant Quicksilver Rearrangement in there as well, that premise of increased fine tuning to one's protean flesh seems like a logical step before.<br /> <br /> In fact, maybe forget the Heart's Blood Charms... oh wait no, Quicksilver Rearrangement isn't the one with the large number of prerequisites, and it does feel as though some Heart's Blood should be included in what is effectively a weird Heart's Blood upgrade (you should be doing <i>something</i> to internalize those plant shapes).<br /> <br /> So it's Essence 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answer! I'll keep it in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1546-great-cthulhu","name":"Great Cthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1546_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}